{"id": "urban-place-two-routes", "title": "One consultant, two routes: paid by the City and by its no-staff grantee", "seconds": 130.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.051, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "62d5e0556de1cef6", "words": 389, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Urban Place is a consulting firm. It sets up and runs business districts.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.22, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "sub": "a Long Beach firm that runs business districts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.56, 0.64, 0.72, 1.2, 1.67, 2.04, 2.33, 2.47, 2.65, 2.93, 3.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "But City money reaches the same firm a second way, through a grantee with no staff.", "t0": 4.34, "t1": 9.57, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Office of Economic and Workforce Development", "sub": "pays the firm"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Mid Market Foundation", "sub": "a City grantee"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "sub": "paid again"}], "kicker": "Two routes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.38, 0.63, 1.07, 1.24, 1.56, 1.91, 2.01, 2.46, 3.18, 3.35, 3.46, 4.11, 4.33, 4.62]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "How much went that way?", "t0": 9.69, "t1": 10.76, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Office of Economic and Workforce Development", "sub": "pays the firm"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Mid Market Foundation", "sub": "a City grantee"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "sub": "paid again"}], "kicker": "Two routes"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.36, 0.53, 0.77]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["oneLine", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "About 1.67 million dollars.", "t0": 10.76, "t1": 13.4, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1,668,521", "label": "paid by Mid Market Foundation to Urban Place"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.04, 0.52, 0.69, 1.02, 1.3, 1.6, 2.0]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 13.92, "t1": 15.57, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.17, 0.3, 0.93, 1.08, 1.18]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "The records show the City’s economic office paid the firm", "t0": 15.79, "t1": 18.55, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "City payments to Urban Place", "rows": [["FY2020", "149000"], ["FY2023", "120000"], ["FY2019", "99500"], ["FY2022", "80000"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.44, 0.6, 0.76, 1.08, 1.68, 2.07, 2.33, 2.46]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "448,500 dollars directly, on five contracts.", "t0": 18.55, "t1": 23.53, "shot": "b4x", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "City payments to Urban Place", "rows": [["FY2020", "149000"], ["FY2023", "120000"], ["FY2019", "99500"], ["FY2022", "80000"]]}, "emph": ["448,500"], "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.62, 1.13, 1.62, 2.02, 2.27, 2.66, 3.44, 3.82, 4.19]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "The same office is the only City funder of Mid Market Foundation.", "t0": 23.65, "t1": 27.25, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Mid Market Foundation", "sub": "only City funder: the economic-development office", "chip": "$26,041,956"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.89, 1.08, 1.26, 1.56, 1.84, 2.21, 2.32, 2.53, 2.85]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "In fiscal 2025 alone, it paid 26,041,956 dollars.", "t0": 27.37, "t1": 31.91, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Mid Market Foundation", "sub": "only City funder: the economic-development office", "chip": "$26,041,956"}, "emph": ["26,041,956"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.39, 0.7, 1.28, 2.15, 2.3, 2.52, 2.76, 3.45, 3.93]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "Most of that went on to street-safety teams. Its biggest contractor was Urban Alchemy, at 25.3 million.", "t0": 32.03, "t1": 38.6, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Urban Alchemy", "sub": "largest contractor, 2024", "chip": "$25,294,208"}, "emph": ["25.3 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.29, 0.44, 0.61, 0.74, 0.82, 1.46, 2.06, 2.5, 2.82, 3.42, 3.58, 3.91, 4.72, 4.87, 5.42, 5.76, 5.96]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "The first lead: the City paid the firm 200,000 dollars to study its district program.", "t0": 38.82, "t1": 44.58, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "ECN CBD BID Impact Analysis", "kicker": "The first lead", "chip": "$200,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.53, 1.41, 1.58, 1.86, 2.0, 2.16, 2.63, 2.78, 3.09, 3.48, 3.93, 4.09, 4.4, 4.61, 5.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "At the same time, the firm was managing one of the office’s grantees.", "t0": 44.7, "t1": 48.06, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "ECN CBD BID Impact Analysis", "kicker": "The first lead", "chip": "$200,000"}, "emph": ["same time"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.2, 0.43, 0.65, 0.81, 1.05, 1.27, 1.64, 1.78, 1.85, 1.96, 2.47]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The second lead is that second route.", "t0": 48.28, "t1": 50.24, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to Urban Place by the Foundation", "rows": [["2024", "811970"], ["2023", "672384"], ["2021", "184167"]]}, "wt": [0.22, 0.28, 0.41, 0.73, 0.91, 1.09, 1.48]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The Foundation paid the firm 811,970 dollars in 2024 alone.", "t0": 50.36, "t1": 56.46, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to Urban Place by the Foundation", "rows": [["2024", "811970"], ["2023", "672384"], ["2021", "184167"]]}, "emph": ["811,970"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.57, 0.71, 0.84, 1.2, 1.49, 1.81, 2.2, 2.79, 3.01, 3.34, 3.81, 4.42, 4.6, 4.83, 5.5]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The Foundation reports zero employees. So who runs it?", "t0": 56.58, "t1": 60.79, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Zero employees", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "emph": ["zero employees"], "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.51, 1.0, 1.44, 2.38, 2.93, 3.1, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Why does the route matter? The grantee buys work the City could buy itself.", "t0": 60.79, "t1": 65.2, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "not subject to the City’s own contracting rules or public contract data"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.47, 0.61, 0.72, 1.03, 1.58, 2.09, 2.56, 2.86, 3.12, 3.23, 3.43, 3.6, 3.8]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "So the City’s own contract rules don’t apply.", "t0": 65.32, "t1": 67.75, "shot": "b11x", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "not subject to the City’s own contracting rules or public contract data"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.23, 0.55, 0.78, 1.3, 1.61, 1.92]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "The third lead: the Foundation’s executive director works 30 hours a week.", "t0": 67.97, "t1": 72.48, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The executive director", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "30 hours a week, $0 pay"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.4, 0.93, 1.43, 1.98, 2.51, 2.99, 3.4, 3.66, 4.05, 4.19]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]"], "text": "And the pay? 0 dollars in every column.", "t0": 72.6, "t1": 75.83, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The executive director", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "30 hours a week, $0 pay"}, "emph": ["0 dollars"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.2, 1.03, 1.47, 2.01, 2.23, 2.63]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[2]"], "text": "How can that be? Another client of the firm explains it.", "t0": 75.95, "t1": 79.33, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "is part of the Urban Place Consulting Group, Inc. team"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.24, 0.46, 1.31, 1.85, 2.16, 2.28, 2.4, 2.7, 3.18]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[2]"], "text": "Its director, with the same name, is on the Urban Place team.", "t0": 79.45, "t1": 82.94, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "is part of the Urban Place Consulting Group, Inc. team"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.79, 0.93, 1.05, 1.36, 2.03, 2.18, 2.3, 2.4, 2.65, 3.05]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "And the firm’s own State filings name a person of that name as its chief executive.", "t0": 83.06, "t1": 87.55, "shot": "b13a", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ir4a", "kicker": "California Secretary of State · 2348819", "text": "Urban Place Consulting Group, Inc.: one person named as chief executive, chief financial officer and director", "mark": "chief executive"}, "emph": ["chief executive"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.29, 0.67, 0.89, 1.2, 1.66, 1.94, 2.02, 2.33, 2.48, 2.74, 3.12, 3.31, 3.48, 3.8]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "story[2]"], "text": "The records do not show whether it is the same person or two people with the same name.", "t0": 87.67, "t1": 92.03, "shot": "b13b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "One name, on both sides", "sub": "no record opened states that the two are the same person"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.44, 0.6, 0.83, 1.12, 1.43, 1.58, 1.72, 1.88, 2.13, 2.6, 2.81, 3.02, 3.33, 3.53, 3.65, 3.97]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[11]", "established[13]", "established[12]", "established[14]"], "text": "The Foundation’s own State filing, from April 2026, names a different chief executive.", "t0": 92.15, "t1": 97.3, "shot": "b13c", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "x24a", "kicker": "California Secretary of State · 4589323", "text": "Mid-Market Foundation, statements of information of 21 October 2024 and 21 April 2026, the only two on file: a different chief executive; neither names the executive director who signed the earlier returns", "mark": "neither names"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.63, 0.85, 1.18, 1.75, 1.92, 2.21, 2.45, 3.51, 3.74, 3.81, 4.2, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "If so, the grantee’s head works for the firm it pays, which approves its own bills.", "t0": 97.42, "t1": 101.59, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Mid Market Foundation", "sub": "pays the firm"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "sub": "employs the team"}, {"art": "question", "name": "The director", "sub": "same name as on the firm’s team"}], "kicker": "The third lead"}, "emph": ["its own bills"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.38, 0.48, 1.01, 1.23, 1.46, 1.59, 1.7, 1.93, 2.12, 2.59, 2.76, 3.14, 3.31, 3.54]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The fourth lead: the Foundation’s return is silent.", "t0": 101.81, "t1": 105.38, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.38, 1.25, 1.65, 2.35, 2.81, 3.04]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "Asked if a management company runs it, it says no.", "t0": 105.5, "t1": 108.27, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No"}, "emph": ["no"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.37, 0.45, 0.91, 1.31, 1.6, 1.96, 2.07, 2.41]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "So a reader can’t learn this 82-million-dollar grantee was run by someone with its consultant’s name.", "t0": 108.39, "t1": 113.73, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "run by a person with the name of its consultant's chief executive"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.28, 0.65, 0.88, 1.11, 1.33, 2.5, 3.1, 3.33, 3.55, 3.69, 4.0, 4.23, 4.38, 4.95]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The records don’t show that the fees were too high.", "t0": 113.95, "t1": 116.33, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That the fees were excessive or the work not done"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.49, 0.67, 0.88, 1.04, 1.21, 1.49, 1.65, 1.85]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[4]"], "text": "Or that City money paid for the same work twice.", "t0": 116.45, "t1": 119.23, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That City dollars paid for the same work twice"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.58, 0.8, 1.04, 1.26, 1.39, 1.51, 1.82, 2.15]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The management deal and the board minutes.", "t0": 119.35, "t1": 122.7, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The management agreement and board minutes"}, {"who": "", "what": "Grant budgets showing the management fee"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.25, 0.56, 0.93, 1.31, 1.8, 2.16, 2.35, 2.46, 2.77]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "And the grant budgets showing the fee.", "t0": 122.82, "t1": 124.76, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The management agreement and board minutes"}, {"who": "", "what": "Grant budgets showing the management fee"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.15, 0.47, 0.9, 1.19, 1.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No authority has ruled on this.", "t0": 124.88, "t1": 126.54, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.54, 0.7, 1.01, 1.19]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 126.66, "t1": 129.47, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.41, 0.55, 0.65, 1.58, 1.86, 2.03]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · paid directly", "lead2": "Lead 2 · the second route", "lead3": "Lead 3 · the unpaid director", "lead4": "Lead 4 · a silent return", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "question"}